        "committer": {
          "name": "Timothy Day",
          "email": "timday@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-23 16:29:30.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-18687 build: add 'make <dir>' for single module directories",
        "message": "LU-18687 build: add 'make <dir>' for single module directories\n\nBuilding one kernel module directory on its own is useful when the\nkernel already carries the rest of Lustre in-tree, e.g. osd-zfs\nagainst an out-of-tree ZFS, or to rebuild a single module quickly.\n\nAdd a 'make <dir>' target for every kbuild directory under lnet/ and\nlustre/ (lnet/libcfs, lustre/osd-zfs, ...). It runs kbuild on the\nwhole tree with LUSTRE_MODULE_SUBDIR set, and the top-level Kbuild\nthen limits obj-m to that directory, so it is compiled with the same\ninclude paths and flags as the full build and no directory needs\nchanges of its own. The directory list is derived from the kbuild\nMakefiles; o2iblnd keeps its dedicated targets.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I768708db62a1659436b813e02632a2f6221b1662\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
